    "markdown": "# 01 · Positioning & Brand Strategy\n### Diyam House of Silver\n\n---\n\n## 1. The positioning statement\n\n> **For the modern Indian woman who wants sterling silver that feels precious — not cheap, not intimidating — Diyam House of Silver is the Bangalore house that makes 925 silver feel like an heirloom you can actually afford. We turn everyday metal into everyday luxury.**\n\nThe name already does heavy lifting: **\"House of Silver.\"** That word *House* is your Tiffany-borrowed asset — it signals a maison, a lineage, a standard. Use it relentlessly. You are not \"a silver shop.\" You are a **House**.\n\n**One-line brand promise (put in bio + pin):**\n*\"925 Sterling Silver, Bangalore. Everyday luxury you can wear, gift & keep forever. ✦ Jayanagar ✦ Ships across India.\"*\n\n---\n\n## 2. The strategic problem we're solving\n\nYour reach is growing (+40%) but engagement is flat (1.3%). Translation: **Instagram is showing your Reels to new people, and they scroll past.** Three fixable causes:\n\n1. **No hook** — Reels open on a product with no reason to stay.\n2. **No story / no save-reason** — captions are stock-availability notes, not content people bookmark or send to a sister.\n3. **No consistent identity** — a viewer can't tell a Diyam Reel from any other silver shop in 0.5 seconds.\n\nThe fix is not more posting. It's **hook + story + a recognisable house look.**\n\n---\n\n## 3. Target audience (in priority order)\n\n**Primary — \"The Jayanagar & Bangalore woman, 22–35.\"** Works or studies, active on Reels, buys silver for herself and as gifts, values aesthetics and \"does it look real/premium?\", price-aware but will pay for quality + trust. Shops both walk-in (South Bangalore) and increasingly online.\n\n**Secondary — \"The gifter.\"** Buying for Rakhi, birthdays, anniversaries, return-gifts, weddings. Occasion-triggered, needs reassurance on quality (925 hallmark), packaging and delivery timelines.\n\n**Tertiary — \"Pan-India silver lover.\"** Discovers you through a viral Reel, buys via DM/website/ships. This is your growth engine — the auto-translation + trend audio unlock this audience.\n\n**What they need to believe to buy:** (1) it's *real* 925 sterling, (2) it *looks* more expensive than it costs, (3) it *won't tarnish/turn skin green*, (4) *delivery & returns are safe*, (5) *this brand has taste.* Every content pillar below answers one of these.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Brand voice\n\n**Warm, confident, tasteful — a stylish elder-sister who knows silver.** Not salesy-shouty. Not stiff-luxury. Premium but reachable.\n\n- **Say:** \"Meet the anklet that goes with literally everything.\" · \"925 sterling. It'll outlive the trend.\" · \"For the sister who steals your jewellery anyway.\"\n- **Avoid:** \"Available in stock. DM for details.\" (dead language), ALL-CAPS spam, over-emoji, \"cheapest price!!!\"\n- **Signature sign-offs to build recall:** *\"— House of Silver ✦\"* · *\"Worn in Bangalore, loved everywhere.\"* · *\"Real silver. Real shine. Real you.\"*\n\n---\n\n## 5. Visual identity (make a Diyam Reel recognisable in 0.5s)\n\nConsistency of *look* is what turns reach into follows. Lock these:\n\n- **Palette:** silver/graphite + one warm accent (deep maroon or champagne) + clean off-white backgrounds. Avoid rainbow thumbnails.\n- **Lighting:** soft, directional, single-source. Silver photographs best with soft window light or one softbox. No harsh flat flash.\n- **Recurring motifs:** a signature surface (marble slab / raw silk / dark velvet), your hands-and-jewellery framing, and a fixed **on-screen text style** (same font, same placement — bottom third, one line).\n- **Cover/thumbnail system:** every Reel cover uses the same font + a 2–4 word title so your grid reads as one designed shelf, not a jumble. This alone lifts profile-visit-to-follow rate.\n- **Logo discipline:** small watermark, bottom corner, never covering the product. Hook first — brand reveal in the last 2 seconds.\n- **Grid rhythm:** think in rows of 3. Alternate: Reel cover · detail shot · lifestyle. The grid is your shop window.\n\n---\n\n## 6. The TWO content engines (your hybrid model)\n\nYou asked for two reference types handled separately. Here they are as two engines you'll alternate inside the same calendar. Roughly **60% Engine A / 40% Engine B** — lead with reach, close with taste.\n\n### Engine A — \"Viral Local\" (reach + sales) · ~60%\n*Inspired by Giri Zever Mahal, Pukhraj, Viral Jeweller, PSG Gold.*\n\n- **Job:** get discovered, grow followers fast, drive DMs/footfall.\n- **Format:** fast, trend-audio, hook-heavy, product-forward, festive tie-ins, price/offer reveals, \"which one would you pick?\", satisfying close-ups, packing/unboxing.\n- **Length:** 7–20 seconds, looping.\n- **CTA:** \"DM 'RAKHI' to order,\" \"link in bio,\" \"save this for later,\" \"tag your sister.\"\n- **KPI:** views, shares, saves, follows.\n\n### Engine B — \"House of Silver\" (positioning + trust) · ~40%\n*Inspired by Tiffany & Co.*\n\n- **Job:** make Diyam feel premium and trustworthy; justify price; build the brand.\n- **Format:** cinematic, slow, story/emotion-led, craftsmanship, \"how we check 925 purity,\" heirloom/gifting stories, founder/atelier moments, styling films.\n- **Length:** 15–45 seconds.\n- **CTA:** soft — \"Discover the collection,\" \"The House of Silver.\"\n- **KPI:** saves, profile visits, comments, brand sentiment, follows from quality viewers.\n\n**Rule of thumb:** Engine A gets them in the door. Engine B makes them respect you enough to buy and stay. Never run one without the other.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Content pillars (what every Reel/post is \"about\")\n\nEvery piece maps to one pillar so the account feels intentional:\n\n1. **Trust & Proof (P1)** — 925 hallmark, purity tests, anti-tarnish, real-vs-fake. *Answers \"is it real?\"*\n2. **Styling & Versatility (P2)** — how to wear it, stacks, one piece 3 ways, GRWM, outfit pairings. *Highest-saving content.*\n3. **Occasion & Gifting (P3)** — Rakhi, Independence Day, anniversaries, return gifts, packaging. *The commercial engine this month.*\n4. **Product Hero / New Drop (P4)** — the satisfying close-up, the reveal, price/offer. *Engine A's bread and butter.*\n5. **Brand & Behind-the-scenes (P5)** — the House story, the atelier, the owner, the packing table, customer love/UGC. *Builds trust + relatability.*\n\nTarget weekly mix: **P2 & P4 heavy for reach, P3 for sales this season, P1 & P5 for trust.**\n\n---\n\n## 8. Profile & bio setup (do this before Day 1)\n\n- **Name field** (searchable — use keywords, not just brand): `Diyam House of Silver | 925 Silver Jewellery`\n- **Bio:**\n  `✦ 925 Sterling Silver · Jayanagar, Bangalore`\n  `Everyday luxury you can gift & keep forever`\n  `Ships across India 🇮🇳 | Rakhi gifting open 🎁`\n  `↓ Shop / WhatsApp to order`\n- **Link:** link-in-bio hub (website + WhatsApp + catalog) — see file 03.\n- **Convert to a Professional (Business) account** if not already — required for Shopping, product tags, Trial Reels, insights, and boosting.\n- **Highlights to create:** *Rakhi* · *925 Proof* · *Styling* · *Reviews* · *Shipping/FAQ* · *Store.*\n- **Pin 3 Reels:** one viral hook, one trust/proof, one Rakhi gifting.\n\n---\n\n*Next: `02_30_Day_Content_Calendar` — the day-by-day build.*\n"
