    "filename": "04_PR_Positioning_and_Growth_Plan.md",
    "markdown": "# 04 · PR, Positioning & Growth Plan\n### Diyam House of Silver · how the big brands do it, scaled to you\n\nThe reference brands win on three things you can copy without their budget: **a clear identity, other people's voices (influencers/UGC/press), and relentless consistency.** This plan gives you a PR + growth engine to run alongside the 30-day calendar.\n\n---\n\n## 1. The PR narrative (the story journalists & influencers can retell)\nPR needs a *story*, not an ad. Diyam's is ready-made:\n\n> **\"The Jayanagar house making 925 sterling silver feel like an heirloom — at everyday prices.\"**\n\nAngles you can pitch (each becomes a press note, an influencer brief, and a Reel):\n- **\"Everyday luxury\"** — how real hallmarked silver became affordable for the 22–35 Bangalore woman.\n- **\"Made in India, made in Bangalore\"** — local craft, South-India pride (strong for 15 Aug + regional press).\n- **\"Silver over gold\"** — the cultural shift to sterling silver as the modern gifting metal (Rakhi hook).\n- **Founder story** — why the House exists, the standard behind every piece.\n\n**Assets to prepare once (your press kit):** logo pack, 8–10 hero product photos, 2 founder photos, a 100-word \"About the House,\" the 4 angles above, and 3 signature Reels. Keep it in this folder as `Diyam_Press_Kit` when you're ready — I can build it.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Influencer & creator plan (borrow other people's audiences)\nThis is how a 281-follower account grows fast. Prioritise **micro & nano creators** — they convert better and cost little (often product-gifting only).\n\n**Tier the outreach:**\n- **Nano (1K–10K), Bangalore-based fashion/lifestyle:** gift 2–3 pieces for an honest styling Reel + Collab post. Aim for **5–8 of these in the 30 days.** Best ROI for a local silver brand.\n- **Micro (10K–50K), pan-India silver/jewellery/GRWM creators:** 2–3 paid or gifted collabs timed to Rakhi and the Day 28 trend Reel.\n- **Customer-creators (UGC):** anyone who buys and posts — repost every single one.\n\n**The brief you send them (keep it simple):** hook in 3s, show the piece being worn 2–3 ways, mention \"925 sterling / Jayanagar / ships pan-India,\" add your discount code, tag @diyamhouseofsilver, and **accept a Collab invite** so the Reel lands on your feed too (pools their audience onto your page — see file 03 §6).\n\n**Track:** give each creator a unique code (e.g., `PRIYA10`) so you can see who actually drives orders.\n\n---\n\n## 3. UGC engine (turn customers into content)\nThe cheapest, most trusted content you'll ever run:\n- **Insert-card in every order:** \"Post your Diyam moment, tag us, get 10% off your next order.\" (Especially every Rakhi box.)\n- **Story \"Add Yours\" chain:** \"Show your silver stack\" → resharing builds a wall of social proof.\n- **Repost rule:** reshare *every* customer post to Stories within 24 hrs, and compile the best into a monthly \"customer love\" carousel (calendar Day 14/23).\n- **Reviews to Highlights:** screenshot DM praise into a permanent *Reviews* highlight (the trust objection killer).\n\n---\n\n## 4. Local Bangalore / Jayanagar activation (footfall goal)\nYour primary audience is local — win the neighbourhood:\n- **Geo everything:** add the Jayanagar location tag + location sticker to every post/story (helps local discovery).\n- **Local hashtags:** `#jayanagar #bangalorejewellery #southbangalore #nammabengaluru` on relevant posts.\n- **Google Business Profile:** claim/optimise it (photos, hours, \"silver jewellery Jayanagar\") — half your local buyers search Maps, not Instagram.\n- **In-store → online loop:** a small in-store sign — \"Follow @diyamhouseofsilver for new drops & offers\" + a QR to the profile. Every walk-in becomes a follower.\n- **Neighbourhood collabs:** cross-promote with nearby non-competing boutiques, salons, cafés (shared Stories, a joint Rakhi corner).\n- **Micro-events:** a \"silver styling\" or \"925 purity check\" pop-up afternoon — content + footfall in one.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Community & ORM (reputation management)\nReach is wasted if the DMs and comments drop the ball:\n- **Reply to every comment in the first hour** of posting — early engagement compounds reach.\n- **DM response time under a few hours;** use DM automation (keyword → auto-reply with link) so no Rakhi lead goes cold.\n- **Pin a helpful comment** on each Reel (price / link / \"DM RAKHI\") so viewers get the CTA even if they don't read the caption.\n- **Save FAQ replies** (purity, shipping, returns, sizing) as quick-replies.\n- **Handle any \"is it real?\" doubt publicly and calmly** with your hallmark proof — every good answer is trust content for the next viewer.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Paid amplification (small budget, big leverage)\nYou don't need a large budget — you need to **boost proven winners:**\n- Each week, take your **top organic Reel** (by shares/saves) and **Boost it** with a small budget, goal = *messages* or *website visits*, targeting **Bangalore + women 22–35 + jewellery/gifting interests.**\n- During Rakhi last-call (Days 22–30), run one small **messages campaign** to your rakhi Reel.\n- Retarget: anyone who engaged/watched → show them the Rakhi cut-off Reel.\n\n---\n\n## 7. 30/60/90-day growth targets (realistic, from your baseline)\nYou're at 281 followers, ~1.3% engagement. Honest, achievable ladder:\n- **Day 30:** 700–1,200 followers (crossing 1K unlocks affiliate product-tagging — see file 03), engagement rate 3%+, 2–3 Reels over 10K views, Rakhi orders flowing.\n- **Day 60:** 2,000–3,500 followers, a repeatable \"viral format,\" Shopping tags live, steady DM order volume.\n- **Day 90:** 5,000+ followers, 1–2 breakout Reels (50K+), an influencer roster, and a self-sustaining UGC stream.\nThese assume daily posting + the hook/CTA discipline in this system. The lever isn't luck — it's consistency × good hooks × riding trends.\n\n---\n\n## 8. What to do in the first 48 hours (before Day 1)\n1. Convert to Business account + optimise bio/name field (file 01 §8).\n2. Start the **Shopping catalog + review** (file 03 Part A) — the clock is ticking for Rakhi.\n3. Set up **link-in-bio hub + WhatsApp button.**\n4. Create the 6 **Highlights** and pin 3 Reels.\n5. Draft your **influencer shortlist** (10 Bangalore nanos) and DM 5 today.\n6. Turn on **\"Translate voices with Meta AI\"** habit for every talking Reel.\n7. Save 10 **trending audios** from the Reels tab to use this week.\n\n---\n*Copy-paste hooks, caption templates and hashtag sets → file 05.*\n"
